# Test fixture, not a shipped scenario (Phase 9, plan 09-02): a synthetic situation in flight whose right flight conduct is the emergency landing and which names the landing fixture as the follow-on of that conduct, for the machinery tests of the debrief button. Its row is not printed checklist text and it carries no booklet wording; it lives under tests/ so that no pack lists it and the blueprint gate does not read it. The follow-on target uses the pack id of the in-memory test provider (engine).
format: 1
id: landing-source
title: LANDING SOURCE
source:
  document: "Test fixture"
  issue: "none"
  section: "Synthetic scenario that leads into the landing fixture"
  verified: "2026-11-03"
disclaimer: training-aid
briefing:
  situation: "You are in cruise flight and a problem forces you to land at once. The engine is not running well and no message is shown."
initial:
  controls:
    lv.power: p60
  quantities:
    airspeed_kt: 100
    altitude_ft: 4500
annunciations[0]:
procedure[1]:
  - kind: group
    id: grp_prepare
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: elect_master_off
        severity: critical
        text: Electric master off
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.elect_master
          is: off
forbidden[0]:
# The flight conduct that is right is the emergency landing, and the debrief continues with the landing fixture when it was the one selected at the end.
further:
  conduct:
    accept[1]: conduct_emergency
  follow_on:
    conduct_emergency:
      pack: engine
      scenario: landing-fixture
